From 6d88287120a6f66218b9849d53052aa95d53245d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 19:50:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recalibrate cannibalization gate: compare ENTITY
 (mold-stripped), not full title
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes systemic lexical false positives found against the real 207-post corpus:
comparing full titles let distinct topics collide on the shared boilerplate mold
("… tem cura? o que esperar do tratamento", "… o que é e como…"), so the gate
would silently reject good posts (status rejected) — the opposite of the goal.

- New additive column blog_post_index.entity_normalized = stripMold(title): the
  title with boilerplate mold phrases removed, leaving the topic/entity. Camada 1
  lexical now compares entity vs entity, so "alcoolismo" vs "bulimia" ≈ 0 while
  true rewordings ("coração acelerado sem motivo" vs "…sem motivo aparente")
  stay high.
- Numbered-variant guard: entities equal except for a number (Bipolar Tipo 1 vs
  Tipo 2, TEA nível 1 vs 2) are distinct topics and never block, in both layers.
- Thresholds env-tunable in prod without a logic redeploy: BLOG_CANIB_LEX
  (default 0.72), BLOG_CANIB_SEM (default 0.90, up from 0.85).
- Report endpoint now returns per-pair `bloquearia` + `numeroDistinto` and a
  `bloqueariaTotal`, computed with the live gate logic, to validate precision
  against the corpus before trusting it.
- migrate adds the column + a GIN(trgm) index on entity_normalized. Re-run
  migrate then reindex-corpus to populate the entity column.

Fail-open preserved throughout. Typecheck + build pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
